From: NavQ95 <navq95@local>
Subject: [PATCH] imx95: navq: keep M7 GPIO2/GPIO5 security config

bl31_plat_arch_setup() forces PCNS/ICNS/PCNP/ICNP of every GPIO port to
non-secure on each A55 boot. On the NavQ the M7 (PX4) owns pins on GPIO2
and GPIO5 and runs them secure; flipping the security bits clears the
pins ICR (irq config) and leaves the M7 stuck in the GPIO irq handler
whenever Linux reboots. Leave these two ports alone.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific configuration]
---
diff --git a/plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c b/plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c
index 5ac95d7d8..8203e5838 100644
--- a/plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c
+++ b/plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c
@@ -102,6 +102,12 @@ void bl31_plat_arch_setup(void)
 
 	/* Assign all the GPIO pins to non-secure world by default */
 	for (unsigned int i = 0U; i < gpio_num; i++) {
+#if defined(PLAT_imx95)
+		/* M7 sets its pins/irq line secure; rewriting this on an A55 reboot wipes its ICRs */
+		if ((gpio_base[i] == GPIO2_BASE) || (gpio_base[i] == GPIO5_BASE)) {
+			continue;
+		}
+#endif
 		mmio_write_32(gpio_base[i] + 0x10, 0xffffffff);
 		mmio_write_32(gpio_base[i] + 0x14, 0x3);
 		mmio_write_32(gpio_base[i] + 0x18, 0xffffffff);
